{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1351238-using-mythic-lands","id":1351238,"title":"Using Mythic Lands","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-27T01:10:25-08:00","id":1351238,"title":"Using Mythic Lands","content":"So here we have that fascinating umbral realm of myth and fiction and very little in rules or discussion about it. With how developed communications are today, a lot of young mages could be using more mythological/fictional characters for their spirit magic rather then crusty and dusty Goetia demons. Adepts of the Silver Portal already do interact with such realms extensively, why shouldn't even more dynamic mages do so? Not to mention quite a few fictional being sort of expect to be summoned and used in such a way like LoL/Dota champions or Fate servants, <br /> <br /> So, how would you go about stating such beings in a game? How much quintessence, how to eyeball power levels, some rules for manifestation, paradox, etc. Maybe what you would think some of those creature's reaction would be to the WoD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T10:14:11-08:00","id":1352028,"title":"","content":"I have no idea what you're talking about. A link? Some more context?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T23:51:51-08:00","id":1352762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1351238-using-mythic-lands?p=1352028#post1352028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea what you're talking about. A link? Some more context?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll try to explain. <br /> <br /> Mages with Spirit sphere can summon various umbrood/spirits/aliens etc. <br /> Generally, it is assumed they either summon local spirits that stay in Penumbra next to the real world or contact various religious beings. <br /> <br /> There is an umbral realm called Mythic Lands. This is where the non-religious figures of various mythologies used to live. However, with the explosion of fiction and communications the Mythic Lands also experienced explosive growth. Now Mythic Lands house Star Wars, Star Track, My Little Pony, etc. Including even more popular fan-works. <br /> <br /> So, why would a modern mage, steeped in modern culture and fiction risk summoning those cranky angels and demons born thousands of years ago? Sure, they would be more powerful and much, much more knowledgeable, but the denizens of Mythic Lands are much more understandable. Lore about them is freely available too! Not to mention some of those beings are pretty much designed to be summoned. The oneiromantic sorcerer tradition of Silver Portal already does that, though mostly treffiking with even more ephemeral creatures. And superman is a paradox spirit, with other superheroes continuously generated from Wyld. <br /> <br /> How I personally would see it that you either need Spirit 3 + Space 3 to drag a stable character from Mythic lands, or Spirit 3 to go there and manually walk one back to Earth. Maybe you could also play around with Life and Prime for more stability. For summoning you would need a correspondence link in the form of a fictional work from which you are summoning it. Also probably divied them in ranks of 1 to 5 as other spirits. The most popular ones like HP could be summoned of any rank, bu the less popular/powerful ones would not get higher ranks. <br /> <br /> <br /> So what are your thoughts about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T14:17:14-08:00","id":1352872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1351238-using-mythic-lands?p=1352762#post1352762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll try to explain.<br /> <br /> Mages with Spirit sphere can summon various umbrood/spirits/aliens etc.<br /> Generally, it is assumed they either summon local spirits that stay in Penumbra next to the real world or contact various religious beings.<br /> <br /> There is an umbral realm called Mythic Lands. This is where the non-religious figures of various mythologies used to live. However, with the explosion of fiction and communications the Mythic Lands also experienced explosive growth. Now Mythic Lands house Star Wars, Star Track, My Little Pony, etc. Including even more popular fan-works.<br /> <br /> So, why would a modern mage, steeped in modern culture and fiction risk summoning those cranky angels and demons born thousands of years ago? Sure, they would be more powerful and much, much more knowledgeable, but the denizens of Mythic Lands are much more understandable. Lore about them is freely available too! Not to mention some of those beings are pretty much designed to be summoned. The oneiromantic sorcerer tradition of Silver Portal already does that, though mostly treffiking with even more ephemeral creatures. And superman is a paradox spirit, with other superheroes continuously generated from Wyld.<br /> <br /> How I personally would see it that you either need Spirit 3 + Space 3 to drag a stable character from Mythic lands, or Spirit 3 to go there and manually walk one back to Earth. Maybe you could also play around with Life and Prime for more stability. For summoning you would need a correspondence link in the form of a fictional work from which you are summoning it. Also probably divied them in ranks of 1 to 5 as other spirits. The most popular ones like HP could be summoned of any rank, bu the less popular/powerful ones would not get higher ranks.<br /> <br /> <br /> So what are your thoughts about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>What book/page reference do you have?<br /> <br /> I would think such a land would have beings in the collective conscious of humanity for centuries, not just a couple decades. So &quot;new&quot; beings there would be stories circulating maybe from the late 1700s, early 1800s at the latest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T15:20:22-08:00","id":1352878,"title":"","content":"Much as I like the idea, I think the denizens of the Mythic Lands are all creatures people BELIEVED were real at one time. Nobody over the age of 10 believes Superman and Harry Potter are real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T13:34:08-08:00","id":1353133,"title":"","content":"","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 12-06-2019, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T13:36:14-08:00","id":1353135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1351238-using-mythic-lands?p=1352878#post1352878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much as I like the idea, I think the denizens of the Mythic Lands are all creatures people BELIEVED were real at one time. Nobody over the age of 10 believes Superman and Harry Potter are real.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what? I mean, even so why does it matter if the people that believe are young? Even if we disregard the difference between conscious belief and subconscious outpouring of creative energy directed at the frendom, millions of children are good enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T14:11:33-08:00","id":1353144,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4340_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4340\" data-vbnamecard=\"4340\">Warpwind</a> life begins when you become a tween...<br /> <br /> Seriously. I do kinda like the idea of pop culture icons becoming mythic beings. But if that\u2019s the case, then literally every fictional character ever created can exist in the Mythic Lands if enough people believe in her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T23:26:20-08:00","id":1353260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1351238-using-mythic-lands?p=1353144#post1353144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4340_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4340\" data-vbnamecard=\"4340\">Warpwind</a> life begins when you become a tween...<br /> <br /> Seriously. I do kinda like the idea of pop culture icons becoming mythic beings. But if that\u2019s the case, then literally every fictional character ever created can exist in the Mythic Lands if enough people believe in her.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say teens is when you properly begin to Sleep. <br /> <br /> yeap. it was mentioned that Mythic Lands were much more stable in middle ages and before, but modern age of hyper-communications caused it to fracture into mess of fandoms and alternate histories formed and supported by the rabid energy of their followers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T15:13:07-08:00","id":1353434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1351238-using-mythic-lands?p=1352872#post1352872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What book/page reference do you have?<br /> <br /> I would think such a land would have beings in the collective conscious of humanity for centuries, not just a couple decades. So &quot;new&quot; beings there would be stories circulating maybe from the late 1700s, early 1800s at the latest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consulting my antique copy of The Book of Worlds, the Mythic Worlds are described on pages 63 - 65. They aren't a single realm, but a descriptor for countless realms born out of human vision and imagination. They start as small micro-realm dream bubbles in Maya/The Dream Realm, and most simply dissolve after a night or so. But ones that keep getting revisited, by either the original dreamer or those that share the idea (or just a very similar one) grow, and eventually turn into full fledged realms. Some of these realms are born out of myths and legends. Others out of what could be described as a cultural zeitgeist or collective ideal. And yes, some do form out of modern fiction. The issue though is that when I say these realms are countless, I'm not exaggerating. And trying to find the specific one you are looking for can sometimes be very difficult. To use Camelot as an example, you can go looking for Malory's version and end up in Twain's. Or in the movie Excalibur. Or the original Welsh story. And so on. The same thing can happen with Star Wars. If you find a realm based on it, is it pre or post Disney? Pre or post prequels? Pre or post Empire Strikes Back? How much expanded universe? Etc. You might even stumble across some obsessive fan's fan-fiction version where Han Solo and Jabba the Hutt are happily married and Luke is an intergalactic pizza delivery boy. And speaking of obsessive fans, one of the types you are most likely to meet in any Mythic Realm based on a fandom are the dreaming fans of that property. And they may react negatively to outsiders who aren't &quot;one of us&quot;. <br /> <br /> Summoning anything from the Mythic Realms is likely to have some of the same issues as finding the realm you want. Summoning Luke Skywalker might end up giving you novice farm boy Luke or cranky old hermit Luke just as easily as it will get you Jedi Knight Luke. Because the Mythic Worlds spawn from Maya, certain issues involving Changeling and its chimera may come in to play, with the unawakened destroying them with disbelief or possibly not even being able to see or interact with them at all. Creatures summoned are likely similar to Bygones, and suffer the same problems many of those beings can have in a reality they don't really belong in. <br /> <br /> As far as who would actually do something like this, Orphans certainly might try it. Hollow Ones also, provided that the fandom or fiction in question is sufficiently &quot;cool&quot;. The Dreamspeakers of the Ghost Wheel Society may have members who study this sort of thing, as might the Baruti. The Hermetic House Thig might also dabble with it, but probably more in counter-culture myths than pop culture fandom. Etherite Ethernauts may also try to study aliens or technology from certain sci fi realms. (I think there is a good argument that the Gernsback Continuum is a Mythic Realm.) The Wu Lung's realm of Kun Lun is actually a Mythic Realm. I think the Sisters of Hippolyta had a similar Realm, but I can't recall off hand and don't have my copy of Book of Crafts handy to check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T16:46:13-08:00","id":1353449,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Warpwind;n1353260]<br /> <br /> I would say teens is when you properly begin to Sleep.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ll agree to disagree \ud83d\ude0a. Though I do like the idea of childlings in Changeling: the Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T04:19:15-08:00","id":1353524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1351238-using-mythic-lands?p=1353449#post1353449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I do like the idea of childlings in Changeling: the Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was always kind of surprised Changeling never had a players guide for Childlings. I keep hoping someone might do one for the STVault.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T18:50:11-08:00","id":1353672,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> or maybe one for tween and teen changelings. They\u2019re not at all the same as wilders in their twenties and thirties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T22:08:40-08:00","id":1353698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1351238-using-mythic-lands?p=1353434#post1353434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the info!<br /> <br /> Also, the problem of identification is somewhat solvable by using the copy of a specific work in question. While mythic beings would indeed have no personal seals, like ones used by other umbrood, the works in question are easily available. So you'll need to get a printout, a book, a disk, maybe some souvenir or paraphernalia as a sympathetic link to the summoned being in question.<br /> <br /> As for the stability (chimera -&gt; umbrood) and problems of quintessence I also agree. Less established/popular settings would be more ephemeral, though I think using Prime for pattern suffusion/stabilization could come in handy, or preparing a body to possess. As for the more stable umbrood, they would be thaumivores and under danger to be disbelieved if too blatant. Though, advantage of modern culture, quite a few could be either easily masked as human or passed through as a costume or cosplay. Many would also have little trouble blending in culturally.<br /> <br /> Heh. Now that i think on it, summoning more ephemeral beings could lead to quite an existential crises. Being created wholesale with preexisting histories and personalities, for many it would be quite a shock to be summoned, or confronting the fact that they aren't 'real' but a loose cloud of quintessence prone to be blown apart, without summoner's support, by actual people looking at them. Or seeing what a horror-show the universe really is out of their small corner.<br /> <br /> I actually first though of this when reading Massasa War. I remember thinking that instead of all those gods and spirits they should have gone for Dr. Van Hellsing and Dracula. Now that would have been a proper mayhem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 12-09-2019, 04:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T17:09:02-08:00","id":1354003,"title":"","content":"Apropos to nothing: Most of the Mythic Realms I tend to use in my games tend to be really broad conceptions of their subjects rather than specific ones, and sometimes this means they will, on occasion, abruptly shift appearance, mood and even genre while characters are there. Some of them incorporate real history with fiction, or are totally ahistorical, drawing on a sort of muddled &quot;pop history&quot;. Realms like Ye Olde England, Columbia, Victoriana, Suburbia, Hollywoodland, The Shojunate, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T21:56:08-07:00","id":1410613,"title":"","content":"Was reading this thread and I had a thought.<br /> <br /> What about an obsessive fan who's a wizard that's fallen in love with a fictional character?<br /> <br /> Could they summon the spirit and stuff them into a human body they created, bind them to it and thus bring them to &quot;life&quot;?<br /> <br /> Obviously would take a lot of spheres to do that Spirit 5, Life 5, Prime 2... would you need Mind as well?<br /> <br /> Lot of ways this could go so badly wrong with the mythic character hating the person who just tore her/him out of their life. Especially if some of the spirits powers are maintained in their new form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 08-27-2020, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T06:32:16-07:00","id":1410668,"title":"","content":"*Spirit 4. Assuming an unwilling spirit that would need to be chained to the body. I don't think Mind would be necessary.<br /> <br /> Usually the spirit powers would, indeed, manifest on the new form - that's actually one of the reasons mages do this kind of stuff (allowing oneself to be possessed by a spirit it's as traditional magic as it gets).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T09:12:32-07:00","id":1410693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1351238-using-mythic-lands?p=1410668#post1410668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Spirit 4. Assuming an unwilling spirit that would need to be chained to the body. I don't think Mind would be necessary.<br /> <br /> Usually the spirit powers would, indeed, manifest on the new form - that's actually one of the reasons mages do this kind of stuff (allowing oneself to be possessed by a spirit it's as traditional magic as it gets).</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you transform the spirit into a human soul, or would that be Archmage level stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T07:08:03-07:00","id":1410840,"title":"","content":"Ehhh...my gut feeling would be to make that Arch stuff.<br /> <br /> But acording to Cruzade core (the part when they talk about creating humans, I think it's in Life 5) you can create a body with a human soul by adding Spirit 5 to the mix. So I think it could be feasible to do that with Spirit 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T07:19:33-07:00","id":1410844,"title":"","content":"There is mention of the Mythic Realms from the Mage point of view tying into things like Sci Fi and modern fiction, and the Mythic realms seems to be the same realm, or at least tied to the same realm, as the Garou Legendary Realm. My guess from a summoner point of view such beings only have substance while in their Mythic Realm pocket Dimension and summoning Godlike beings into other parts of the Umbra or the Material World from the Mythic Realm results in phantoms or ghosts of their true potence as they are essentially beings of Fictional potential. I would wager summoning them makes them closer to Chimera, as I believe the Mythic Realm/Legendary Realm seems to be tied with the Dreaming and possibly even Arcadia itself. When the Changelings started rumors about Fimbul Winter comings and closing down Arcadia and end snuffing out magic in the Autumn World the Garou noticed the Final Winter arrive in the Legendary Realm, and the Legendary Realm also seemed to be sieged by Fomorians and Jotun similar to the fears about Arcadia.<br /> <br /> I think the more Real you make people from far off fantasies will directly correlate with how Unreal you make local reality in the Tellurian they interact with. It sounds like the start to Mauraderdom, essentially plucking random figments of the imagination and prescribing them greater reality then the objective reality everyone else experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T08:43:28-07:00","id":1410851,"title":"","content":"Note also that WoD isn't as adamant about how special the human soul is as the Chronicles of Darkness are: you could probably take a human-like spirit from the Mythic Realms, put it in a human body, and have something that's indistinguishable from a regular human. Such a creature could potentially even Awaken: there are, after all, artificial humans who have done exactly that. For example, the Sons of Ether Tradition Book includes Frankenstein's monster (if I recall correctly) as an Awakened Etherite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T17:31:06-07:00","id":1410908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1351238-using-mythic-lands?p=1410851#post1410851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note also that WoD isn't as adamant about how special the human soul is as the Chronicles of Darkness are: you could probably take a human-like spirit from the Mythic Realms, put it in a human body, and have something that's indistinguishable from a regular human. Such a creature could potentially even Awaken: there are, after all, artificial humans who have done exactly that. For example, the Sons of Ether Tradition Book includes Frankenstein's monster (if I recall correctly) as an Awakened Etherite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like your saying that the Order of Hermes should conscript the spirits of Harry Potter characters into the order then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T14:07:14-07:00","id":1411118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1351238-using-mythic-lands?p=1410613#post1410613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was reading this thread and I had a thought.<br /> <br /> What about an obsessive fan who's a wizard that's fallen in love with a fictional character?<br /> <br /> Could they summon the spirit and stuff them into a human body they created, bind them to it and thus bring them to &quot;life&quot;?<br /> <br /> Obviously would take a lot of spheres to do that Spirit 5, Life 5, Prime 2... would you need Mind as well?<br /> <br /> Lot of ways this could go so badly wrong with the mythic character hating the person who just tore her/him out of their life. Especially if some of the spirits powers are maintained in their new form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see this as the basis for any number of Marauder characters. &quot;Obsession to the point of belief in things that just aren't so&quot; fits quite well into their purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12765-otto-d-fey","name":"Otto D'Fey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T20:25:48-07:00","id":1411156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Otto D'Fey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1351238-using-mythic-lands?p=1411118#post1411118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could see this as the basis for any number of Marauder characters. &quot;Obsession to the point of belief in things that just aren't so&quot; fits quite well into their purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>That can certainly work for Marauders, but obsession doesn't necessarily mean irrational insanity. <br /> <br /> Voormas was beyond obsessed with death and immortality and he didn't become a marauder. <br /> <br /> If a Mage has the spheres, there's nothing that out there conceptually with going to the Mythic Lands and capturing the spirit you want to bind into the body you created.<br /> <br /> Of course, a mage with the spheres to pull that off is probably old enough that he doesn't care about Harry Potter, but Princess Leia or Elvira, Mistress of the Dark, or what have you are possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T20:25:48-07:00","id":1411157,"title":"","content":"Double Post. Not sure how that happened.<br /> <br /> Is there a delete option that I'm missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}